Chromel ships a compiled snapshot of filter lists that other people wrote and
maintain.  Nothing in `blocklist.txt` is ours.

Source rulesets: https://github.com/uBlockOrigin/uBOL-home
  uBOL is licensed GPL-3.0.  The rules in `chromium/rulesets/main/` are compiled
  by that project from the lists below.

Underlying lists:
  EasyList            https://easylist.to/            CC BY-SA 3.0
  EasyPrivacy         https://easylist.to/            CC BY-SA 3.0
  uBlock filters      https://github.com/uBlockOrigin/uAssets   GPL-3.0

What Chromel does: `scripts/ubol-to-blocklist.py` reads the DNR JSON that uBOL
publishes and rewrites it as one line per host rule.  No rule is added, removed
or reinterpreted; rules that need a matcher we have not built yet (paths,
substrings, regular expressions) are dropped and counted in the file header.

Attribution for the CC BY-SA lists travels with this file: if you redistribute
`blocklist.txt` or a build containing it, keep this notice and the source URLs.

`cosmetics.txt` is derived from the same uBOL snapshot (its compiled
selector lists) and carries the same licenses.
